1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Accessibility barriers can break a user journey
even when a page still looks finished.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
AccessPatch finds a controlled problem,
repairs it, and proves the result.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,500
Here is one React checkout journey.
I use only the keyboard

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:25,000
to add the sample product, open checkout,
enter synthetic data,

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,500
and move to the primary action.
The email field shows visible text,

6
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:38,000
but it has no programmatically associated accessible name.
The primary action receives keyboard focus,
but no visible focus cue appears.

7
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The form still reaches confirmation.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
AccessPatch records barriers in the real journey state,
not only in isolated components.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
The evidence contains exactly two findings.
Axe reports one label violation on the email field.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Browser evidence records no visible outline
or box shadow on the focused button.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
One bounded GPT-5.6 call reviewed this evidence
with store false.

12
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
It used 2,444 recorded tokens
and selected two allowlisted repair strategies.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
It did not write or directly apply source code.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Deterministic templates perform the repair
in a disposable copy.

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,000
One associates the visible email label with the input.

16
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
The other removes only the controlled rule
that suppresses the focus indicator.

17
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,500
The same journey is replayed after repair.
It reaches confirmation,

18
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:45,000
axe reports zero violations, and keyboard focus
has a visible solid three-pixel outline.

19
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The original fixture remains unchanged.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:56,000
The fifteen-file Proof Bundle connects the findings,
repair plan, exact diff, replay, audit records,

21
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,000
and human-review boundaries.

22
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Its report shows the before and after states
and three source-backed WCAG mappings,

23
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
without claiming certification.

24
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,500
As a prevention bonus, Mutation Guard injects
one controlled aria-hidden regression

25
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:23,000
into another disposable copy.
AccessPatch detects it once,

26
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:28,000
preserves the original fixture,
and cleans the temporary runtime.

27
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Codex was the primary engineering environment.
Under human coordination,

28
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,500
it implemented most code, tests,
security hardening, review, and reproducibility work.

29
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:42,000
The final suite has 178 API-free tests,
an eight-stage Judge Workflow,
and a successful seventeen-stage clean-clone verification.

30
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
AccessPatch remains a controlled demonstration.
Human accessibility review is still required.
